This violates equality and ordering because `NaN < anything` and `NaN !== NaN`.

Fix by validating components before comparing, or explicitly defining their behavior:

```js
function compareVersions(a, b) {
  const len = Math.max(a.length, b.length);

  for (let i = 0; i < len; i++) {
